1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:01,050
How fast can

2
00:00:01,080 --> 00:00:02,830
a whole town freeze?

3
00:00:03,370 --> 00:00:04,480
Day three.

4
00:00:04,510 --> 00:00:06,800
Snow falls in the dark.

5
00:00:07,340 --> 00:00:08,060
The power grid

6
00:00:08,090 --> 00:00:09,770
dies, state by state.

7
00:00:10,310 --> 00:00:11,930
People burn their furniture

8
00:00:11,960 --> 00:00:13,070
to stay warm.

9
00:00:13,610 --> 00:00:14,780
Mara's woodpile

10
00:00:14,810 --> 00:00:16,670
lasts four more days.

11
00:00:17,210 --> 00:00:18,050
But four days

12
00:00:18,080 --> 00:00:19,530
is not seven.

13
00:00:20,070 --> 00:00:21,210
Then she checks the ground

14
00:00:21,240 --> 00:00:23,290
sensor under the station.

15
00:00:23,830 --> 00:00:24,820
Forty feet down,

16
00:00:24,850 --> 00:00:26,860
it's still thirty-eight degrees.

17
00:00:27,400 --> 00:00:28,450
Deep down, the Earth

18
00:00:28,480 --> 00:00:29,790
keeps its own heat.

19
00:00:30,340 --> 00:00:31,570
Rule number two:

20
00:00:31,600 --> 00:00:33,260
follow the heat.

21
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:36,230
On her map, one place glows:

22
00:00:36,260 --> 00:00:37,790
Eagle Hot Spring.

23
00:00:38,330 --> 00:00:39,380
Twelve miles

24
00:00:39,410 --> 00:00:40,540
of deep snow.

25
00:00:41,080 --> 00:00:42,310
She builds a sled

26
00:00:42,340 --> 00:00:43,500
from an old door.

27
00:00:44,040 --> 00:00:46,080
Ember's paws are freezing,

28
00:00:46,110 --> 00:00:47,990
so she makes him boots.

29
00:00:48,530 --> 00:00:49,910
Day seven arrives.

30
00:00:49,940 --> 00:00:51,550
It's minus seventeen.

31
00:00:52,090 --> 00:00:53,020
They set out at six,

32
00:00:53,050 --> 00:00:54,580
into a blizzard.

33
00:00:55,120 --> 00:00:59,530
Part three. The hot spring. Follow for part three.
